From: At30c <PabloAtsoc9993@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] m21s: restart Keymaster and Keystore after TEE is ready

Keystore2 and the legacy Keymaster service belong to early_hal and can start
before the F415F TEEgris daemon establishes its secure-world session.  The
previous `start keystore2` action is a no-op when the process is already alive,
leaving it indefinitely blocked without publishing IKeystoreService/default.

Once TEEgris reports Ready, restart Keymaster 4.0 and then Keystore2 so both
reconnect against the now-available secure-world transport.

--- a/etc/init/teegris_v3.rc
+++ b/etc/init/teegris_v3.rc
@@ -21,7 +21,8 @@ on property:vendor.tzdaemon=Ready
     setprop vendor.TEEGRIS.loaded true
     write /proc/iccc_ready 1
     start tzts_service
-    start keystore2
+    restart vendor.keymaster-4-0
+    restart keystore2
 
 on property:vendor.tzts_daemon=Ready
 
